---
description: FlowCRM project development rules
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read docs/PROJECT_PLAN.md before making architectural changes.
- Use Java 21 and Spring Boot for the backend.
- Use React, TypeScript and Vite for the frontend.
- Follow controller-service-repository layering.
- Use DTOs for API requests and responses.
- Never expose JPA entities directly from controllers.
- Validate all user input.
- Use Flyway migrations rather than Hibernate schema generation.
- Never hardcode secrets, database passwords or JWT keys.
- Keep secrets in environment variables.
- Do not delete or rewrite existing working functionality without explaining why.
- Implement one feature at a time.
- Run relevant tests after each implementation.
- Before modifying more than five files, describe the planned changes.
- Never commit or push code unless explicitly instructed.
